text.section:
The Board may grant, without examination, a restricted license for a temporary appointment to teach dentistry at a dental school in this Commonwealth to any person who:

Is a resident of a foreign country;


Is licensed to practice dentistry in a foreign country;


Holds a faculty appointment in a dental school in a foreign country;


Is a graduate of a foreign dental school or college or the dental department of a foreign institution of higher education;


Is not licensed to practice dentistry in Virginia;


Has not failed an examination for a license to practice dentistry in this Commonwealth;


Has received a temporary appointment to the faculty of a dental school in this Commonwealth to teach dentistry;


Is, in the opinion of the Board, qualified to teach dentistry; and


Submits a completed application, the supporting documents the Board deems necessary to determine his qualifications, and the prescribed fee.
